/* ==========================================================================
 * AU_UNIVERSITIES -- education provider directory dataset
 * --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * 1258 providers on the **Commonwealth Register of Institutions and Courses
 * for Overseas Students (CRICOS)**, the Australian Government register
 * published as open data at data.gov.au (dataset
 * e5ae7059-bfa8-4fa4-a5c0-c13cf3520193). Generated by
 * _tooling/build_dataset_au.py -- do not hand-edit.
 *
 * WHY EVERY PROVIDER HERE CAN ENROL YOU
 *
 * Under the ESOS Act 2000 a provider may not offer a course to a student-visa
 * holder unless the provider and the course are both registered on CRICOS, and
 * the Confirmation of Enrolment a subclass 500 application is built on can only
 * be issued against a CRICOS course code. Being on this list is therefore
 * exactly the permission the cards state as "Intl. Admits: Yes" -- it is not an
 * inference. Providers whose only registered courses are compulsory schooling
 * are excluded (this page is about tertiary study), as are providers with no
 * live registered course.
 *
 * FIELDS
 *
 *   name      the registered institution name, with the legal-entity suffix
 *             and any bracketed acronym moved out for display. The `cricos`
 *             field carries the provider code(s), which are the unambiguous key.
 *   capacity  the provider's REGISTERED OVERSEAS-STUDENT CAPACITY -- the
 *             maximum number of overseas students CRICOS permits it to enrol.
 *             This is a real published figure off the register. It is a
 *             ceiling, NOT an enrolment count and NOT an acceptance rate, and
 *             the UI labels it "CRICOS capacity" for that reason. (The UK page
 *             carries an invented `offerRate` in this slot; this page does not
 *             repeat that.)
 *   programs  the three commonest fields of education across the provider's
 *             live registered courses, using the register's own ASCED broad
 *             field classification. Indicative, and derived from real data.
 *   type      "Group of Eight" for the eight members of the Go8; "University"
 *             for the other institutions in TEQSA's Australian University
 *             provider category; then "Higher Education", "Vocational" and
 *             "English & Pathway" by the highest AQF level the provider holds
 *             a live registered course in.
 *   location  the greater capital city where the registered postcode falls in
 *             one (Australia Post ranges), otherwise the register's own
 *             locality, plus the state or territory.
 *   rank      entries 1-36 are the Australian institutions in the QS World
 *             University Rankings 2026, in QS order. Everything after that is
 *             ordered by type tier then name and carries NO ranking meaning;
 *             `ranked` is false for those and the UI shows a dash.
 *   alt       searched, never rendered: trading names, campus cities and the
 *             short forms applicants type. All but a handful come from the
 *             register itself.
 * ========================================================================== */

